Package: mica-system
Version: 1.0.1-1
Source-Date-Epoch: 1789603200
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: systemd, systemd-sysv, systemd-resolved, systemd-repart, systemd-timesyncd, udev, dbus, kmod, dropbear-bin, procps, nftables, passwd, quota, e2fsprogs, dmsetup
Description: Mica OS board-independent system policy
 The system half of every Mica OS root: the DATA layout and project quotas,
 the seed and reconcile tools under /usr/lib/mica with their units, the bind
 mounts of /mica, /mica/containers, /srv, /home, /root, /var, /var/lib/mica,
 /etc/hostname and /usr/local/lib/systemd/system, the health gate and the
 boot-failure handler, the offline provisioning import, the default DHCP
 network, volatile journald storage and the network time policy.
 .
 Enablement is payload: the wants-links and /dev/null masks this package ships
 are the whole of it, and no maintainer script enables a unit. The presets
 50-mica-dropbear.preset and 50-mica-nftables.preset keep dropbear.service and
 nftables.service disabled; the postinst refuses a root in which either is
 linked.
 .
 SSH is dropbear.service, started by micad at runtime scope once it has written
 /run/mica/dropbear.env. The unit requires that file and a listener in it, runs
 after mica-shadow-reconcile.service, and keeps the ed25519 host key on
 DATA/state, made at its first start.
 .
 /etc/shadow is built in RAM at every boot from the image's factory copy, every
 account locked; a transient root password set through micad lasts until the
 next boot.
 .
 The postinst creates the operator account mica, uid and gid 1000, home
 /home/mica on DATA, shell /bin/bash, with no supplementary groups and no
 password.
 .
 nftables is the firewall tooling; this package ships no ruleset. dmsetup is
 the device-mapper tool and udev rules for the verity root. procps provides ps,
 top, free and kill. passwd provides the tools the postinst runs.
